---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Exercise 12 - Identifying the Most Common Employment Type for Data Analyst Positions

Business Problem:
The recruitment team wants 
to understand which employment type is most common among Data Analyst job postings. 
This insight will help prioritize future hiring strategies and recruitment campaigns.
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------


SELECT COUNT(job_title_short) AS Total_Job_Posting, 
       job_schedule_type,
       ROUND(COUNT(*) * 100.0 / SUM(COUNT(*)) OVER(), 2) AS Percentage
FROM job_postings_fact
WHERE job_title_short = 'Data Analyst' 
  AND job_schedule_type IS NOT NULL
GROUP BY job_schedule_type
ORDER BY Total_Job_Posting DESC;

-- Business Insight:
-- Full-time represents 86.48% of all Data Analyst job postings,
-- making it by far the most common employment type.
